{
 "_note": [
  "Placed wall and building pieces per map, read from the cooked World Partition cells (static mesh instances) of the world each map uses, with the mesh material slots (component overrides applied) resolved to a physical material through the material parent chain.",
  "A piece is one placed instance of a static mesh. Wall and building pieces are meshes under Environment/Architecture, ExternalAssets, Props/Walls_and_Fences and Transport_Infrastructure/Road_Barriers. Distant-view (HLOD) proxies, foliage, landscape, roads, props and traversal-only collision blocks are not counted.",
  "pieces_with_material counts pieces whose mesh has that physical material in at least one material slot, so a piece with two materials is counted under both and the rows add up to more than the total. slot_split_share divides each piece equally over its slots (slot surface areas are not in the data) and adds up to the total. \"none\" is a slot with no physical material set anywhere in its parent chain (mesh decals).",
  "scope \"play\" keeps pieces whose component centre lies inside the bounding box of the map zone-region polygons plus 500 m on each side; scope \"world\" is the whole world package. Saburtulo has no region list, so only its world scope exists. Positions are in centimetres, world coordinates. Component centres are used, not individual instances (inferred approximation).",
  "Built area is the 1st to 99th percentile of placed building positions (kilometres, world coordinates), not a measured map border.",
  "Extractor method: round 65 (docs/evidence/round65-open-questions.md)."
 ],
